lt like  maybe this is my next thing you know  like maybe helping entrepreneurs is my  next next big move maybe that's what I'm  really you know that's my real passion  and only three people showed up and it  was really disheartening and I felt like  at that time and this is this is a total  failure right like I was flown in this  event the YMCA was phone in the event  and  and nobody shows up for a free thing how  am I ever going to charge for how am I  ever gonna make money how am I ever  going to turn this into a career and I  decided in that moment that would keep  going right that I would help those  three people and it just felt so amazing  helping those people seeing their eyes  light up having them leave the room  feeling not just motivated encouraged  but also having ideas that they could go  and actually now build their business  and knowing that I had an impact that  that meant something real to me and I  knew that I had to find a way to keep  going it was from that moment it may  become so alive that I had to find a way  to keep doing this and I didn't care if  I way didn't care but I didn't know if  I'd ever make money I didn't know if I'd  ever be successful in that but I knew  that I loved it so much i just i love  that high of helping entrepreneurs that  i had to find a way to keep doing it  even if that meant doing some other  things well i tried to figure out my  path i would for sure keep this as one  of the things that I did so that was I  think the biggest struggle for me was  just knowing that I love something and  knowing how excited i got buy it but not  knowing how I'd ever turn it into a  business not knowing how I never support  myself doing this and because I loved it  because it was genuine I kept doing it  and I kept doing more presentations and  more events and all of them for free  because I didn't have a business model  behind it that just I fed off the energy  and it started to grow and I had you  know five people the next one at ten  people the next 12 15 and 20 and 30 and  50 and it just kept growing and then  launched my website and then I got asked  to speak at different events and then I  started to get paid to speak and wasn't  a lot of money a couple hundred dollars  maybe but like wow you want to pay me to  calm sure happy to and then I started  increasing my speaking fee and a lot of  it is because while i was driving more  awareness i was building up a name for  myself and to with more practice I got  better right my my speeches now are way  better than they were at the start and  so I can justify charging a lot more  money now than I could when I first  started and it gradually grew from there  and I think YouTube was one of the when  I started on YouTube and when I really  went all in on YouTube that's when it it  hit me that i'm finding something i  absolutely love doing because i would  answer emails for people and i would  spend i would spend like an hour writing  somebody back an email if you ask me  this question i would spend an hour  sitting there writing an email to  respond to you and I was getting too  many emails and I'm much more of a  visual person I thought why don't I turn  this into a video i started my channel  and you guys have been the fuel to keep  me going and i'm responding the videos  and making you guys grow your businesses  and giving you helpful advice and tips  and wisdom and ideas and that has now  accelerate my business where i'm getting  opportunities with brands i'm getting  international speaking deals and i have  a book deal and so I face the same  challenge that a lot of you guys are  facing now we're at the beginning you  have this love you have this passion  excitement for something that you're  doing and you don't know how you're  gonna make it work and you feel  everything that you try doesn't bring in  enough dollars to support yourself and  the key is just to keep going if you  keep going you will figure it out and  all the plans that I had y